From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 13:39:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt7988a: update ethernet node for NETSYS v3 driver

Update the MT7988A SoC dtsi for the NETSYS v3 ethernet driver:

- ethernet: extend the clock list (SGMII tx/rx, USXGMII/SGMII
  selectors, XFI PHY xtal, MACSEC), name the FE and PDMA interrupts
  (fe0-3/pdma0-3), add the SRAM region and phandle, and reference the
  sgmiisys/usxgmiisys syscons, TOPRGU (watchdog) and HWVER syscons
  used by the driver.
- watchdog: add "syscon" compatible so the ethernet reset logic can
  access TOPRGU through a regmap.
- topmisc: move the register base to the start of the block and extend
  its window to the full 64K while retaining the dedicated syscon node.
- power controller: add a logical provider which references the topmisc
  syscon and supplies the TOPS0/TOPS1 domains.
- xsphy: rebase the xphyu3port0 mediatek,syscon-type offset from
  topmisc+0x194 to topmisc+0x218 so it still resolves to the same
  absolute register (0x11d10218) after the topmisc base moves.
- cpus: describe the shared L2 cache (next-level-cache on all four
  cores, cache-unified) and add #cooling-cells = <2> so a board
  thermal zone can bind the CPUs as a cooling device.
- add the hwver syscon node.

The added clock names are only required by the MT7988 SoC data
(required_clks); other NETSYS generations keep their existing device
trees. Pairs with the mtk_eth_soc NETSYS v3, PCS and MT7988 pmdomain
patches in this series.

Signed-off-by: Sean McCully <sean_mccully@yahoo.com>
